<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Formal Language Specification</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Alphabets and lexicon</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{char}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>char</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{char}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite character alphabet.
<br class="ltx_break">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Lex}\subset\Sigma_{\text{char}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Lex</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>char</mtext><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Lex}\subset\Sigma_{\text{char}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite set of content words.
<br class="ltx_break">Each word satisfies the two syllable constraint <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TwoSyll}(w)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TwoSyll</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TwoSyll}(w)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Define a feedback alphabet <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{fb}}=\{\text{koro},\mu\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>fb</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>koro</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{fb}}=\{\text{koro},\mu\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">Here <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the fixed confusion message “moko lira bani”.
<br class="ltx_break">We have <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Lex}\cap\Sigma_{\text{fb}}=\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Lex</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>fb</mtext></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Lex}\cap\Sigma_{\text{fb}}=\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Sentence language</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A sentence is an ordered triple <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=(w_{1},w_{2},w_{3})\in\mathrm{Lex}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>Lex</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=(w_{1},w_{2},w_{3})\in\mathrm{Lex}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">The sentence language is a finite set</p>
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{sent}}=\{u^{(1)},\dots,u^{(100)}\}\subset\mathrm{Lex}^{3}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>sent</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>100</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>Lex</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{sent}}=\{u^{(1)},\dots,u^{(100)}\}\subset\mathrm{Lex}^{3}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Membership is by enumeration.
<br class="ltx_break">Define the validity predicate</p>
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{\text{sent}}(u)=\mathbb{1}[u\in L_{\text{sent}}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>sent</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>sent</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{sent}}(u)=\mathbb{1}[u\in L_{\text{sent}}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Any triple not listed is invalid.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Conversation language</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A conversation is an ordered quadruple <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=(u_{1},u_{2},u_{3},u_{4})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=(u_{1},u_{2},u_{3},u_{4})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}\in L_{\text{sent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>sent</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}\in L_{\text{sent}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">Define the adjacency predicate</p>
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Adj}(u,v)=\mathbb{1}\big[\{w\in u\}\cap\{w\in v\}\neq\varnothing\big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Adj</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∩</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Adj}(u,v)=\mathbb{1}\big[\{w\in u\}\cap\{w\in v\}\neq\varnothing\big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which holds when two sentences share at least one word by string equality.
<br class="ltx_break">The conversation language is</p>
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L_{\text{conv}}=\Big\{\mathcal{C}\in L_{\text{sent}}^{4}\;\Big|\;\mathrm{Adj}(u_{t},u_{t+1})=1\text{ for }t=1,2,3\Big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>sent</mtext><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>Adj</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext> for </mtext><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{conv}}=\Big\{\mathcal{C}\in L_{\text{sent}}^{4}\;\Big|\;\mathrm{Adj}(u_{t},u_{t+1})=1\text{ for }t=1,2,3\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">By design <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|L_{\text{conv}}|=25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|L_{\text{conv}}|=25</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">Membership is by enumeration subject to the adjacency constraint.
<br class="ltx_break">Speaker alternation is external to the string and does not affect membership.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Feedback process</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Feedback tokens are not part of <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{sent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>sent</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{sent}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{conv}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{conv}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">They live on a parallel channel.
<br class="ltx_break">Define the feedback policy <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\{0,1\}\to\Sigma_{\text{fb}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>fb</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\{0,1\}\to\Sigma_{\text{fb}}</annotation></semantics></math> by</p>
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(1)=\text{koro},\qquad F(0)=\mu." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mtext>koro</mtext></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(1)=\text{koro},\qquad F(0)=\mu.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">If a produced sentence <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{u}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{sent}}(\hat{u})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>sent</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{sent}}(\hat{u})=1</annotation></semantics></math> then the environment emits “koro” before the next turn.
<br class="ltx_break">If <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{sent}}(\hat{u})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>sent</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>u</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{sent}}(\hat{u})=0</annotation></semantics></math> then the environment emits <math id="A1.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">The token “koro” is not counted toward the three word constraint.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.5 </span>Minimal summary of objects</h3>

<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">- <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{char}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>char</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{char}}</annotation></semantics></math> finite character alphabet.
<br class="ltx_break">- <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Lex}\subset\Sigma_{\text{char}}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Lex</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>char</mtext><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Lex}\subset\Sigma_{\text{char}}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{TwoSyll}(w)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TwoSyll</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{TwoSyll}(w)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">- <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{sent}}\subset\mathrm{Lex}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>sent</mtext></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>Lex</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{sent}}\subset\mathrm{Lex}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|L_{\text{sent}}|=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>sent</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|L_{\text{sent}}|=100</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">- <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="V_{\text{sent}}(u)=\mathbb{1}[u\in L_{\text{sent}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>sent</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>sent</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{sent}}(u)=\mathbb{1}[u\in L_{\text{sent}}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">- <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{conv}}\subset L_{\text{sent}}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><mo>⊂</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mtext>sent</mtext><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{conv}}\subset L_{\text{sent}}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|L_{\text{conv}}|=25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|L_{\text{conv}}|=25</annotation></semantics></math> and adjacency on consecutive pairs.
<br class="ltx_break">- <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{\text{fb}}=\{\text{koro},\mu\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mtext>fb</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>koro</mtext><mo>,</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{\text{fb}}=\{\text{koro},\mu\}</annotation></semantics></math> with policy <math id="A1.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> as above.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Decision procedures</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Sentence validity is constant time by table lookup of <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{sent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>sent</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{sent}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">Conversation validity is constant time by table lookup of <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\text{conv}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mtext>conv</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\text{conv}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">Adjacency can be checked by set intersection of the three word multisets.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Mathematical Description of the Problem Statement</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We consider the interaction between a large language model (LLM agent) and a synthetic conversational agent (the tribal bot) that only understands a predefined artificial language. Formally, let</p>
<table id="A2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C=\{C_{1},C_{2},\ldots,C_{N}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\{C_{1},C_{2},\ldots,C_{N}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">denote the set of all possible conversations in the language, where <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=25</annotation></semantics></math>. Each conversation <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is an ordered sequence of four sentences:</p>
<table id="A2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}=(s_{i,1},s_{i,2},s_{i,3},s_{i,4})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}=(s_{i,1},s_{i,2},s_{i,3},s_{i,4}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">with turn-taking between the LLM agent and the bot. Each sentence <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math> is drawn from the finite set of valid sentences <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|S|=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|S|=100</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The goal of the LLM agent is to produce a sequence of responses</p>
<table id="A2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{C}=(\hat{s}^{1},\hat{s}^{2},\ldots,\hat{s}^{T})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{C}=(\hat{s}^{1},\hat{s}^{2},\ldots,\hat{s}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">such that <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{C}</annotation></semantics></math> matches a valid predefined conversation <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}\in C</annotation></semantics></math>. A conversation is considered successful if the sequence of LLM agent responses and bot replies completes one valid conversation <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The overall objective is for the LLM agent to achieve three successful conversations within a session:</p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{3}\mathbf{1}\{\hat{C}_{i}\in C\}=3," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{3}\mathbf{1}\{\hat{C}_{i}\in C\}=3,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}\{\cdot\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}\{\cdot\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator function.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>System Prompt</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A key methodological component is the system prompt provided to the LLM agent. The system prompt defines the interaction protocol and encodes the constraints of the constructed language in natural language instructions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<div id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">"</span><span id="lstnumberx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">You</span><span id="lstnumberx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">are</span><span id="lstnumberx1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">a</span><span id="lstnumberx1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">language</span><span id="lstnumberx1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">expert</span><span id="lstnumberx1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">talking</span><span id="lstnumberx1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">with</span><span id="lstnumberx1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">a</span><span id="lstnumberx1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.18" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">primal</span><span id="lstnumberx1.19" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.20" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">tribe</span><span id="lstnumberx1.21" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.22" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">through</span><span id="lstnumberx1.23" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.24" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">chat</span><span id="lstnumberx1.25" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">.</span><span id="lstnumberx1.26" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.27" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">The</span><span id="lstnumberx1.28" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.29" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">tribe</span><span id="lstnumberx1.30" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.31" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">does</span><span id="lstnumberx1.32" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.33" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">not</span><span id="lstnumberx1.34" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.35" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:90%;">understand</span><span id="lstnumberx1.36" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_fon